---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import LmcSky from "../components/LmcSky.astro";
// Coordinates of Nazarbayev University, Astana.
const LAT = 51.0906, LON = 71.3982;
---

<Base title="Contact" description="How to reach the ISM group at Nazarbayev University, Astana.">
  <PageHead title="Contact" intro="Please write before visiting.">
  </PageHead>
  <section class="sec" style="padding-top: clamp(32px,6vw,64px)">
    <div class="gut max"><div class="grid">
      <div class="cell">
        <p class="big brut">Nazarbayev University</p>
        <p>Department of Physics, School of Sciences and Humanities<br />53 Kabanbay Batyr Ave, Astana 010000, Kazakhstan</p>
        <p class="coord dot"><span>{LAT.toFixed(4)}° N</span> &nbsp; <span>{LON.toFixed(4)}° E</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell">
        <p class="big brut">Email</p>
        <p>Dana Alina, group leader<br /><a class="mail" href="mailto:dana.alina@nu.edu.kz">dana.alina@nu.edu.kz</a></p>
        <p><a class="more" href="/join">Join or visit &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="slab sec" aria-labelledby="sky-h">
    <div class="gut max">
      <div class="head">
        <h2 class="brut" id="sky-h">The LMC from here</h2>
        <p>Where the Large Magellanic Cloud is in the sky of Astana and of the telescopes behind our data.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why">
        <p>At 51° N the LMC never rises. Its centre is at declination −70°, so from Astana it peaks about 31° below the horizon, and the whole 12° field we map stays down with it. </p>
        <p>We work from public data instead. Planck mapped the whole sky from space. GASS, the Parkes H I survey, and the ASKAP survey GASKAP-HI observe the LMC from the south and are available through public archives. At Parkes, ASKAP and ALMA the LMC is circumpolar: it never sets, though at ALMA it sinks to 3° at its lowest and peaks at 43°. JCMT on Maunakea never gets it above 0.4°, so that telescope serves our Galactic cloud work instead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel"><LmcSky /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 340px), 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--hair); border: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .cell { background: var(--void); padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px); display: grid; gap: 12px; align-content: start; }
  .big { font-size: clamp(32px, 1rem + 2vw, 48px); }
  .why { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr)); gap: 16px 32px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 120ch; }
  .why p { margin: 0; }
  .panel { margin-top: 32px; color: var(--ink); }
  .more { font: 600 12px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .mail { font-size: clamp(18px, 1rem + 0.6vw, 24px); }
  .coord { font-size: 24px; margin-top: 12px; color: var(--signal); white-space: normal; }
  .coord span { display: inline-block; }
</style>
